# No active Trivy ignores.
#
# Keep this file so CI and local supply-chain scans can pass --ignorefile
# consistently. Trivy ignores use one finding ID per line (vuln CVE/GHSA IDs,
# misconfig IDs like AVD-*, or secret rule IDs). Add an entry only with a
# tracked owner + reason, e.g.:
#
#   CVE-2026-XXXXX  # Owner: <name>. Not exploitable because <justification>.
#   AVD-AWS-0123    # Owner: <name>. Accepted risk: <why>.
#
# Note: the secret scanner allowlists well-known EXAMPLE values (e.g.
# AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE); use realistic high-entropy values when validating
# detection, or a test will show zero findings and look broken.
